WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.450
This year is the year

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:05.520
that you start doing yoga,
and I mean for real this time.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.730
You're going to join the
36 million-plus Americans

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.230
who have taken up this beautiful practice,

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.240
connecting yourself with
a millennia-old tradition

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.460
and helping you flush out
those nasty toxins, or,

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:19.880
you know, probably not.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.250
Before you grab a mat,
here's what yoga really does

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.773
to your body and brain.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.660
First of all, yoga comes in
many, many different styles,

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.650
but generally speaking, it involves

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.860
some amount of stretching and meditation.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.840
Now, despite what you may have read,

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.790
there's no scientific
evidence to support the idea

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.900
that yoga will flush out
toxins from your colon

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.330
or anywhere else.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.690
But that doesn't mean these techniques

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.900
can't help your body in many other ways.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.980
Take back pain for instance.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.300
An estimated 80% of Americans

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.000
will suffer from back pain
at one point in their lives.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.140
But one study found that after
just six to 12 yoga sessions,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.370
participants reported significantly

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.720
less pain in their lower back.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.420
That's because certain yoga poses

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.530
stretch out your hamstrings,
which, when they're too tight,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.490
can yank on your hip flexors
and strain your lower back.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.370
But the more you practice yoga,

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.650
the more flexible your hamstrings get.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.910
For example, in a 2015
study, women practiced

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.860
a type of hatha yoga,
which involves positions

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.690
like downward dog and triangle pose.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.920
They practiced 90 minutes each week

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.220
for around 16 weeks straight.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.900
And by the last week, they could reach

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.010
four centimeters closer
to their toes than before

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.860
thanks to those loose hamstrings.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.210
Now, if you're also meditating
during those yoga sessions,

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.350
the flexibility might
not be the only benefit.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:52.920
After seven to 16 weeks
of meditative activities,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.990
participants in one study saw a huge drop

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.130
in C-reactive proteins in their blood.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.940
Those proteins are linked to inflammation,

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.960
which, when you're overly stressed,

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.030
can kick into overdrive.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:07.750
And over time, that inflammation

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.060
may contribute to serious illnesses

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.180
like cardiovascular disease and cancer.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.040
That's where yoga's
meditative qualities can help.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.770
Researchers suspect that
yoga may reduce stress

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.990
by interfering with the
central nervous system's

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.950
ability to release stress hormones.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:27.660
Plus, studies show that
meditation-focused types of yoga,

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.200
like yoga asana, boost
levels of feel-good hormones

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.010
like oxytocin in the brain.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.710
Plus, yoga is an exercise,

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.990
and exercise in and of
itself is a stress reliever.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.830
In fact, the US Department
of Health and Human Services

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.670
recommends two and a
half to five hours a week

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.720
of light to moderate exercise.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.790
That can include workouts like yoga,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.130
brisk walking, or swimming.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:52.740
And to be fair, any
amount of regular exercise

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.160
is most likely going to reduce anxiety,

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.810
elevate mood, and improve
sleep and self-esteem.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.490
So while yoga might have an edge

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.610
in the flexibility department
and mindfulness department,

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:07.670
there are plenty of other
activities you can try to get fit.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.410
But as long as it gets you moving

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.350
and maybe gives you some new friends,

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:12.553
why not give it a try?

